    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\$4053.70$ per year.",
      "worked": "Petrol:\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{8.6\\text{ L}}{100\\text{ km}}&=\\frac{x\\text{ L}}{35\\,000\\text{ km}}\\\\\nx&=\\frac{8.6\\times35\\,000}{100}\\\\\nx&=3010\n\\end{align*}$$\nAnnual petrol consumption is $3010\\text{ L}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\text{Petrol cost}&=3010\\times\\$1.87\\\\\n&=\\$5628.70\n\\end{align*}$$\nElectric:\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{18\\text{ kWh}}{100\\text{ km}}&=\\frac{x\\text{ kWh}}{35\\,000\\text{ km}}\\\\\nx&=\\frac{18\\times35\\,000}{100}\\\\\nx&=6300\n\\end{align*}$$\nAnnual electricity consumption is $6300\\text{ kWh}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\text{Electricity cost}&=6300\\times\\$0.25\\\\\n&=\\$1575\\\\\n\\text{Annual savings}&=\\$5628.70-\\$1575\\\\\n&=\\$4053.70\n\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
